The report orders `states:` outer-graph-first, not by the manifest's own key order — the fixture
declares the subgraph's `step` machine ahead of the outer `main` one, and the report still puts
`main` first.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-order/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-order
title: Order
summary: Outer-plus-subgraph fixture for playbook-state.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-order/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  intake: []
  step-pipeline:
    dependencies: [intake]
    state: step
    graph:
      spec: []

states:
  step:
    artifact: steps/{instance}/index.md
    initial: spec-ing
    statuses:
      spec-ing:
        transitions:
          - to: done
            when: spec written
      done: {terminal: true}
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: done
            when: intake complete
      done: {terminal: true}
